                    {
                        "sense_id": "84bd0c58-829d-3f02-9f87-d2d3d461f4d6",
                        "entry_id": "15219bf7-eac3-3446-bc4f-ea21b8b9ae11",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Exhibiting or pertaining to transversality; connecting heterogeneous elements (fields, kinds of people, etc)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f54eabb8-08f1-44b6-9d8e-e14f6632f50c",
                                "sense_id": "84bd0c58-829d-3f02-9f87-d2d3d461f4d6",
                                "text": "This kind of politics acknowledges what Yuval-Davis characterizes as transversal feminism which, much like the second wave feminist standpoint theory, “aims to be an alternative to the universalism/relativism dichotomy […]\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19765082-9b34-47f6-a861-eec2bebcae54",
                                "sense_id": "84bd0c58-829d-3f02-9f87-d2d3d461f4d6",
                                "text": "First, transversal feminist activism rests on an understanding of structures and relations of power as pervasive, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
